   "notes": "Partial: no source in the pool gives an API-only run-rate. The total denominator is pinned (company-to-investor $65B at end-July, known in the KB's red-team notes; a >$100B pace by mid-September, new but only via a VC blog relaying the NYT/Axios), and the API share is bracketed by third-party estimates: Sacra/SaaStr 70-75% API (already in the KB's red-team notes, row A9), SemiAnalysis 75-85% with consumer subscriptions ~5% (new). The KB's V-ANT line still multiplies a $30B April run-rate, although KB red-team files already hold $47B, $65B, Q1/Q2 revenue, a $100-120B year-end expectation and the gross-accounting caveat. Unverifiable: all four Reuters URLs returned 401 (c4, c7, c16, c24, c30, c41, c60, c62, c65; Wayback holds only the 401 page). Axios returned 403 to curl and WebFetch, so c44 and c48 are unverifiable, though their figures ($11.5B Q2, $4.73B Q1) check out on other pool pages. The US News copy of the Reuters story (r16) timed out. c54 cites revenuememo.com without www, which has no DNS record (the www page states the same 10-15%). getpanto.ai (r9, r13) returned 503; r23 and r30 have no readable body. Stale or contradicted figures seen on rid pages and not credited: meridian48 (r11) puts 2026 revenue at ~$6.5B; r6, r12 and r27 still carry a $20-26B calendar-2026 estimate that H1 actuals ($4.73B + $11.5B) make implausible; getlatka (r19) says $5B. The SemiAnalysis page behind c23 also says Anthropic's API revenue grew about 13x year on year (not a pool claim). Cids marked irrelevant are customer counts, named customers, compute deals, subprocessors and the web-search price, none of which bears on the API share or run-rate."
