   "notes": "Answered: the tool fee is pinned on every surface. Claude API web search is $10 per 1,000 searches plus tokens, the same as at launch (2025-05-07); web fetch costs tokens only. New to the KB: Google Cloud's own pricing page lists Claude web search at $10 per 1,000 searches, and Anthropic's pricing doc says Foundry and Claude Platform on AWS usage is rated at the Claude API's per-model and per-feature rates, then billed in $0.01 CCUs (the KB already notes CCU billing for Claude Platform on AWS, but not Foundry or the rate basis). Bedrock has neither tool; Google Cloud has basic web search and no fetch; Azure-hosted Foundry has the basic versions. 2026 billing changes, none to the tool fee: free code execution with search or fetch and dynamic filtering (2026-02-17), response_inclusion (2026-06-11), Sonnet 5's $2/$10 made standard (2026-08-10), refusal billing (2026-09-24), and Foundry's move to CCU billing. The rate cards date that move: the 2026-05-12 card applies CCU invoicing to Claude Platform on AWS only; the 2026-07-24 card adds Foundry. Neither card prices the web tools; both point to the pricing docs. I read the two PDFs by decoding their text layer. Errors: c13 dates the free-code-execution change to 2026-05-04, but the release notes put it on 2026-02-17 (May 4 was Workload Identity Federation). c24 says no public Google or Microsoft figure exists; its cited page gives no number, and Google's own pricing page (c56) lists $10 per 1,000, so the claim is also wrong. c2 and c44: the Finout page never mentions web fetch or 2026 changes. c3 and c20: the Spheron pages don't mention the web tools, and Bedrock doesn't offer them. c4: DevelopersDigest gives no tool prices, and says Azure-hosted deployments lack server-side tools, which conflicts with Anthropic's and Microsoft's docs. c16 and c23 are compound claims whose second halves (the basic-only version; AWS's own web search) aren't on the cited page. c26 attributes to Google's docs a statement that sits on Anthropic's web-fetch page; the fact itself checks out."
